  16. Backfill / Live Indexer Race

  The advisory lock pg_try_advisory_xact_lock(728341003, schemaKey) excludes a concurrent second BackfillAddressDistribution call. It does NOT and cannot serialize against the live indexer (Store.ApplyBlock/RollbackTo), which does not hold or contend for this advisory lock.

  Correctness hole analysis: If the operator runs backfill-address-distribution while the indexer is running, the backfill transaction sees a consistent REPEATABLE READ snapshot of addresses at the moment it opens its transaction. Meanwhile, the live indexer continues committing incremental distribution deltas. After the backfill commits, the live indexer's deltas are relative changes on top of whatever was in the distribution table at commit time — they don't know the backfill just overwrote the base, so the bucket values will be inconsistent with the current addresses state.

  Classification: This is an operational trust boundary — the same documented requirement as backfill-accounting and backfill-supply-rollup. The operator is instructed to stop the index process first. The advisory lock is honest: it prevents concurrent backfill, not live-indexer contention. The usage doc string in cmd/qoge-explorer/main.go and distribution_backfill.go's comment both state this requirement explicitly. This is acceptable as a precondition, consistent with existing conventions, not a code defect. NON-BLOCKING OPERATIONAL TRUST-BOUNDARY NOTE.

